The source commit was cherry-picked with -s -x and changes only internal/vm/task_test.go.
It preserves the exact final request-count, task ID and ExecID assertions.

The mock records each Wait request before sending an optional buffered notification
for that exact task/exec identity. The lifecycle test registers each notification
before launching its process and awaits it with a stopped five-second timer after
cancelling the request context. The test then follows its existing I/O and exit
sequence. No sleeps or production behavior changes were added. DeleteProcess still
waits for I/O completion independently of the asynchronous monitorExit goroutine.

Actual validation from the exact clean source revision:
- Plain and race test binaries compiled with -mod=readonly, and go vet passed.
- Targeted TestTaskManager_CreateExecDeleteTask passed 25 repetitions for each of
  eight combinations: root/nonroot x GOMAXPROCS=1/default x plain/race (200 total).
- No failures, skips or race warnings. Source remained clean before/after tests.
- Existing prior documentation/functional heads are ancestors, not replaced.
  go.mod, go.sum, versions.json, dependency references and prior receipts are unchanged.
- No full VM rebuild, runtime suite, vHive deployment, CRI/native-restore test, global
  installation, matrix run or observation was performed for this maintenance.
  Prior functional acceptance remains tied to its original source and artifact hashes.

Baseline limitations and main evidence:
The lead confirmed the original c4ae5f3 CI timing failure: PopWaitRequests saw one
request while two monitor goroutines were expected to have entered Wait. This task's
300 bounded local pre-fix repetitions passed, so the sporadic failure was not locally
reproduced. Earlier milestone branches did not rerun a pre-fix baseline.
Main patch validation passed 800 targeted repetitions across all eight combinations,
plus all 22 internal/vm tests under -race as root and nonroot (no skips). A clean
committed build at 426c7f5 passed 40 further race repetitions. Those main results are
separate from the 200 repetitions on this branch. Two initial main baseline harness
invocations used incorrectly ordered env options and exited 127; their original logs
remain retained. Corrected commands passed and only 300 valid attempts are counted.
